winebus: turn off a pad nobody is using.

A DualSense that connects over Bluetooth while wine already holds it gets no
macOS GameController plugin, so macOS's 900 s idle cut never applies to it,
and in every such connection retained the pad did not turn itself off after
its usual eleven minutes either. Left alone it runs flat.

WHAT WAS MEASURED, from macOS's and Steam's own logs:

- 2026-09-12/13: connected at 23:28:10 with a game holding it; the game and
  Steam were gone by 00:07:48; the pad dropped by itself at 03:21:07 and the
  next connection reported 0 % battery -- 3 h 13 min with, very likely, no
  wine process left;
- 2026-09-13: the same, for 27 minutes after wine exited at 22:15:44;
- 2026-09-14, a pad macOS was driving: off by itself after 686 s.

THE MECHANISM, measured on 2026-09-14 on a DualSense Edge (054c:0df2) over
Bluetooth with no wine running: IOHIDDeviceSetReport with feature report
0x08 of 48 bytes -- 08 02, zeros, and the Bluetooth CRC-32 (seed 0x53 over the
first 44 bytes) little-endian in the last four, e0 ef a2 23 for this content.
Opened shared it returned 0 and bluetoothd logged the pad's own disconnect
(HID reason 431, ACL 10719) 63 ms after the Set report; opened with
kIOHIDOptionsTypeSeizeDevice, as winebus opens it, it returned 0 and the
disconnect came 64 ms after. Both times the light went out and the pad stayed
off until PS was pressed.

THE CHANGE, in bus_iohid.c. A started DualSense on Bluetooth that this
process holds seized is sent that report once, after IdlePowerOffMinutes (a
REG_DWORD per model key beside SeizeDevice; absent: 20, 0: never, otherwise
clamped to 5..240) with no stick, trigger or button input. Activity is
measured against the last report that counted: sticks and triggers when they
move more than 4, the button bytes on any change, the counter bits of the
short 0x01 masked off, gyro, accelerometer, battery and touchpad ignored.
The report is sent after iohid_cs is released, with the IOHIDDeviceRef
retained, so a pad turning itself off cannot hold up iohid_device_stop. The
request is not repeated; a reconnect is a new device with a fresh clock. A
FIXME, visible without +hid, says when it acts and what IOKit returned.

NOT CLAIMED: that it was measured inside wine;
that a game takes the pad back after PS reconnects it; that a pad held still
in the hand, or used only for motion or the touchpad, is in use; anything
after wine exits, which is where the reported drain happened.

